A1. Do this and you're apt to get yourself in a hole. ~ DIG
A4. This is something about the ladies. ~ CAPE
A8. A distress signal. ~ SOS
A11. This is always going abroad. (Abbr.) ~ SS
A13. This fellow was the "only man in the world" to his girl. ~ ADAM
A15. The visitor's baby. ~ BRAT
A17. Reno is good for this. ~ SPLIT
A19. One having a terrible disease. ~ LEPER
A21. This has the last word. ~ ECHO
A23. Having a strong flavor showing origin. ~ RACY
A24. Southern girls and very sweet stuff. ~ LASSES
A26. Malted milk should make you think of this name. ~ HORLICK
A28. New York's favorite son. ~ AL
A29. Something easy, something soft. ~ SNAP
A31. To get together. ~ UNITE
A33. Feminine name. ~ HATTIE
A35. The king catcher. ~ ACE
A36. Masculine pronoun. ~ HE
A37. Rooters. ~ HOGS
A38. Lessen. ~ ABATE
A40. It takes a wide-awake person to do this. ~ SEE
A41. Smoke; vapor. ~ FUME
A42. No wide-awake person would do this. ~ SNORE
A43. A fish. ~ SHAD
A44. This grows on you. ~ AGE
A45. An age that was hard on the feminine sex. ~ STONE
A46. They say it's easy to get this in Chicago. ~ SHOT
A47. Part of the verb "to be." ~ IS
A48. The yellow dog. ~ CUR
A49. An American. ~ YANKEE
A52. Panaceas. ~ CURES
A54. A skin you love to touch—but not pay for. ~ SEAL
A55. Article. ~ AN
A56. This sort of thing isn't very deep. ~ SURFACE
A58. Accompany, wait on. ~ ATTEND
A60. Another thing the contented cow gave us. ~ CALF
A61. Fashioned; formed. ~ MADE
A63. Wild; timid. ~ EERIE
A64. Frequently. ~ OFTEN
A66. A limited period. ~ TERM
A68. You must get up to do this. ~ RISE
A69. Pronoun. ~ WE
A70. What all vaudeville performers consider themselves. (Theatre slang.) ~ WOW
A71. Where the flappers like their sheiks. ~ NEAR
A72. Boy's nickname. ~ NED

D1. A lot of people get "roped" in this town. ~ DALLAS
D2. What most people have, but seldom get. ~ IDEAL
D3. Wide open spaces. ~ GAPS
D5. For which some fathers send their boys to college. ~ AB
D6. Before (prefix). ~ PRE
D7. Several people designated individually. ~ EACH
D9. High-hat word for what you often swallow when you eat fish. ~ OS
D10. Hallowe'en habitué. ~ SPRITE
D11. What pickles and ice-cream make you. ~ SICK
D12. Where the future ham sandwiches grow. ~ STY
D14. What a messenger boy carries on his hip. ~ MESSAGE
D16. How your great-grand-daddy addressed your great-grandma. ~ THOU
D18. High-brow "cheese-cloth." ~ LACE
D20. One good reason to "own your own home." ~ RENTS
D22. Adorned. ~ ORNATE
D25. What you've seldom done in the subway. ~ SAT
D27. Cockroaches' second cousin. ~ LICE
D30. A device that makes life in an apartment house miserable after dark. ~ PIANO
D32. What the little flowers come from. ~ SEED
D33. Where married men are afraid to g after dark. ~ HOME
D34. Dark stuff. ~ EBONY
D36. You can have a hot time with this. ~ HEAT
D37. What women are stingy with and bears all too generous. ~ HUGS
D39. Length times width. ~ AREAS
D40. What most people always get their foot into. ~ SHOE
D41. What peroxide has made a lot of girls. ~ FAIR
D42. An overgrown babbling brook. ~ STREAM
D43. This is over your head. ~ SHELTER
D45. Comes with every high-class ocean. ~ SURF
D46. This puts the skids under you. ~ SKATE
D48. This brings you to Vertical 33. ~ CURFEW
D50. A news-gathering service (initials). ~ NEA
D51. Why, of course! ~ INDEED
D52. A belief. ~ CULT
D53. Greeting to the family kitten, snoozing on your Sunday coat. ~ SCAT
D55. This one's quite spicy! ~ ANISE
D56. What no prize beauty is at a stag dinner ! ~ SAFE
D57. The first piece of real estate. ~ EDEN
D59. From whence N.Y. gets all its cops and stale jokes. ~ ERIN
D60. Without which there'd be no horizontal 60. ~ COW
D62. Before. ~ ERE
D65. What some girls mean when they say "no." ~ NO
D67. Pa's room-mate. ~ MA


